      "id": "pf_3e96c7a0_value",
      "label": "Paragraph3 — Value",
      "default": "Please kindly note that the battery life is influenced by three main factors: battery capacity, ambient temperature, and power consumption.<br> <br><strong>Battery Capacity</strong><br>Venustas offers three types of batteries, with the largest being the <strong><a href=\"https://venustasofficial.com/products/venustas-7-4v-12v-battery-pack-10000mah\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color: rgb(237, 108, 51);\">Venustas-10000</span></a></strong>. This is the highest capacity battery on the market, rated at 7.4V@10,000mAh(=3.7V@20,000mAh), comparable to 5V@20,000mAh batteries available today. Under constant ambient temperature and power consumption, a larger battery capacity means longer usage time.<br>\n<br><strong>Ambient Temperature</strong><br>At room temperature, the battery can discharge 100% of its capacity. However, at -10°C (14°F), the battery discharges only about 70% of its capacity, and at -20°C (-4°F), it discharges around 50% of its capacity. Thus, using the same battery with the same product in different temperatures can lead to a difference in usage time of up to 1 to 1.5 times.<br>\n<br><strong>Power Consumption</strong><br>Under constant ambient temperature and battery capacity, larger heating elements in heated garment consume more power, which leads to quicker battery drain and shorter usage time. This means that a garment with 6 heating elements will have a battery life about 0.5 to 1 times shorter than one with 3 heating elements.<br> <br>Below is a table showing the usage times for the three types of Venustas batteries, calculated based on a 7.4V heated apparel with 5 heating elements,&nbsp;all tested at room temperature."
    },
